      "passageHtml": "<div class=\"source-doc\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:1.05em;line-height:1.73;color:#292723;overflow-wrap:anywhere\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #bcb5aa;padding:17px 19px;margin:5px 0 20px;background:#fff\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px\">OAKRIDGE (November 22)—Oakridge authorities were notified yesterday that intercity express bus operator Swiftbus <strong style=\"font-weight:800;white-space:nowrap\">143. -------</strong> service to its stop in the city. The company specified December 1 as the effective date of the change. Located in front of Oakridge Plaza, the soon-to-be <strong style=\"font-weight:800;white-space:nowrap\">144. -------</strong> stop was added to the line running between Bealett and Knappton earlier this year. <strong style=\"font-weight:800;white-space:nowrap\">145. -------</strong> In the notice, Swiftbus cited low ridership as the reason for the decision. <strong style=\"font-weight:800;white-space:nowrap\">146. -------</strong> also expressed a willingness to reestablish service to the city if there is an increase in demand in the future.</p></div></div>",
